Apple today released watchOS 27.2, the first major update to the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/watchos-27/">watchOS 27</a> operating system.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1051912" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/watchos-27.jpg" alt="" width="1319" height="742" /><br/>
<br/>
watchOS 27.2 can be downloaded through the Settings app on the watch or the Apple Watch app on a connected iPhone. Software can only be installed when the Apple Watch is on the charger and has over 50 percent battery.<br/>
<br/>
According to Apple's release notes, watchOS 27.2 introduces new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI features and extends &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI to new languages.<br/>
<blockquote>This update provides enhancements to Siri AI, including the ability to retain useful context from previous Siri interactions, draw from a wider range of personal context, and deliver faster responses on your watch. This update also includes other features, bug fixes, and security updates for your Apple Watch.<br/>
<br/>
- Siri AI can recall your past conversations, so you can ask Siri about something it told you before, like the restaurants it recommended last week<br/>
- Siri AI can draw from more sources to give you a great answer, including photos attached in Messages, Calendar event attendees, your voicemails, and better results from Safari history and Reading List from your phone<br/>
- Excluded Apps lets you choose which apps Siri, Search, and suggestions can access, all from one setting on your phone<br/>
- Siri AI now provides faster responses on Apple Watch<br/>
- Siri AI is available in more languages, with support for French, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese, and Spanish. Siri AI is not available in the EU or mainland China</blockquote><br/>
